## 1. Final UI Design Implementations

### Dedicated Ground Stations Network (`/ground-stations`)
Implemented to 100% design parity against [`design/Ground Stations.png`](file:///c:/Users/RH364/OneDrive/Desktop/orbital%20desktop/design/Ground%20Stations.png):
- **Integrated 3D Coverage Mini-Globe**:
  - Embedded Three.js Earth globe rendering active downlink arcs and ground station beacons across Bangalore, Houston, Toulouse, and Canberra.
  - Quick-switch station selector pills on the globe viewport bottom.
- **Selected Ground Station Card**:
  - Highlighting station status (`ACTIVE / NOMINAL`, `DEGRADED`), connected spacecraft (`SAT-001 ORION`, `SAT-003 AURORA`), and real-time signal quality progress gauge (e.g. `98%`).
  - Contact scheduling boxes: `CURRENT CONTACT` (UTC) and `NEXT WINDOW` with dynamic amber countdown (`-01:23:05`).
  - **`DIAGNOSTICS`** button triggering an S-band radio frequency sweep simulation.
- **Global Station Network Ledger**:
  - Comprehensive table tracking Station ID, Location, Link Status, Connected Satellite count, Signal %, and Last Contact timestamp with CSV export capability.

### Live Encrypted Communications Console (`/communications`)
Implemented to 100% design parity against [`design/Live Comunications.png`](file:///c:/Users/RH364/OneDrive/Desktop/orbital%20desktop/design/Live%20Comunications.png):
- **Active Targets Pane**: Lists constellation satellites with live telemetry link status (`CONNECTED`, `WARNING: HIGH LATENCY`, `LOS`).
- **Encrypted Command Terminal**:
  - Live bidirectional message stream with `UPLINK ESTABLISHED` and glowing `SECURE LINK` badge.
  - Interactive telecommand dispatch bar with priority selection (`NORMAL`, `HIGH`, `EMERGENCY`) and simulated satellite acknowledgment callbacks.
- **Communication Metrics**:
  - Graphical 5-bar signal strength meter (`-62 dBm`), latency meter (`124 ms`), uplink lock indicator (`2025.5 MHz`), and AES-256 cryptographic verification.
- **Communications Event Log**: Real-time audit log with search filtering and CSV ledger export.

